{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1448414-help-me-workshop-some-plot-points","id":1448414,"title":"Help me workshop some plot points","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-13T06:30:11-07:00","id":1448414,"title":"Help me workshop some plot points","content":"I need help workshopping some plot elements for a short Dragon-Blooded game I am contemplating. There is a beginning, a middle, and an end, but it need it to connect a little better: <br /> <br /> 1) The PCs work for the Wyld Hunt and they have tracked down the whereabouts of an infamous Abyssal anathema in the far North, near a well-defended mining community nominally allegiant to the Realm. <br /> <br /> The game starts in medias res with the PCs aboard an airship when, out of the mist, three airships appear, carrying the dastardly Abyssal sky pirate and his crew. Between two ships, a beautiful young captive is chained. A fight ensues, the PCs win, the Abyssal will try to escape, and hopefully the captive is freed and brought back to the mining community. <br /> <br /> 2) This section of the game will be centered on roleplaying, investigation, and powering up. A couple of main points they will learn: <br /> <br /> 2a: The captive is a Fae-Blooded prince. And his fae parent is angrily amassing an army to attack the mining community. <br /> <br /> 2b: The fae attacking was the Abyssal's endgame all along. <br /> <br /> 2c: There is a First Age weapons cache hidden somewhere nearby. If used by the PCs, these weapons will provide the leg-up they will need to withstand the approaching army. <br /> <br /> 2d: There is a second Abyssal working with first one. <br /> <br /> 3) The Fair Folk army arrives, there is a battle, and hopefully the PCs will be successful in fending off the invaders using their new weapons. The town is saved and the Fae-Blooded prince is finally free. <br /> <br /> Thoughts and questions: <br /> <br /> X: I am guessing the Abyssal is also after the weapons cache. But where are these weapons kept that the Abyssal will find it the best solution to have a Fair Folk army ravage the town to get to them? And how do the Dragon-Blooded PCs access the cache without ravaging everything? <br /> <br /> Y: I am thinking that something similar has probably happened to the Fae-Blooded prince before, i.e. he is kidnapped or runs away and his force-of-nature parent comes to claim him back. It is a narrative that repeats itself over and over again, leaving ruined Townshend in its wake. The Abyssal knew this when he kidnapped the prince. If the PCs contemplate returning the prince to his parent, the prince will tell them that he does not want to return to that horrible place and that it will not deter his parent from attacking the community, the fae will be able to sense that he was here. Does this hold up? If not, can you help me make it hold up? <br /> <br /> Z: My plan is for the original Abyssal to escape and for there to be a second Abyssal, but I am honestly not sure what I want to do with them. Maybe it is just that is unsatisfactory to triumph over the Fair Folk with no chance to bring justice to those actually responsible for the whole affair in the first place. Can I do anything with one or more Abyssals towards the end? Or is it better to complete skip the second one and use the original one as a set-up for a future adventure assuming he manages to escape?<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],